{
  "dom_id": "step-q4957",
  "name": "Question 20",
  "problem": "For the functions $h(x)$ and $z(x),$ you're given the following data:\n\n$$\nh(5)=5,\\,{h}^{′}(5)=-3,\\,z(5)=-6,\\,{z}^{′}(5)=8\n$$\n\nIf $w(x)=(h(x)+z(x))(3h(x)-10)$, compute ${w}^{′}(5).$",
  "worked_solution": "The product rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(uv)=u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=h(x)+z(x)$ and $v=3h(x)-10.$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}={h}^{′}(x)+{z}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=3{h}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}^{′}(x) & =u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =({h}^{′}(x)+{z}^{′}(x))(3h(x)-10)+(h(x)+z(x))(3{h}^{′}(x)) \\\\  & =({h}^{′}(x)+{z}^{′}(x))(3h(x)-10)+3{h}^{′}(x)(h(x)+z(x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=5$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}^{′}(5) & =({h}^{′}(5)+{z}^{′}(5))(3h(5)-10)+3{h}^{′}(5)(h(5)+z(5)) \\\\  & =(-3+8)\\cdot (3\\cdot 5-10)+3\\cdot (-3)\\cdot (5+(-6)) \\\\  & =5\\cdot 5+3\\cdot (-3)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =34.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
